Hi, I’m Karan!

I’m a high school senior in San Francisco, and I’m obsessed with so many things.

At heart, I’m a writer. I started writing a journal that I share with my dad, and I’ve never really stopped. I currently serve as San Francisco’s first-ever Youth Poet Laureate. I love poetry, but honestly, [anything with a pen and paper](/writing) is my cup of tea!

In addition to writing, I love [building things and gaining experience](/cv). I spend a lot of my week around robots and building cybersecurity solutions for robots. Funnily enough, many of the lessons I’ve learned in poetry translate to robotics! I am also a huge board game enthusiast, and that’s translated into my work with [playkits.org](https://playkits.org) and providing children with safe and healing spaces to play.

There are also always new things that I can’t stop learning about, so I keep a running list of [things I’m chasing now](/now).

In my free time, I love going on my morning run, making pizza, and playing the guitar.

Thanks for reading this far. Feel free to poke around or [say hi](mailto:kgupta1219@gmail.com).

Best,\
Karan Gupta
